event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"## 1\n\nHey, I'm so sorry you're at this point. If it’s been miserable"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" for months, I completely understand why you just want to rip the band-aid off. \n\nBefore you hand in your notice tomorrow, can"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" we talk tonight? I want to make sure you have an exit plan so you’re walking away on your own terms rather than purely"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" out of exhaustion. But if it’s genuinely destroying your mental health and you just can’t walk in there again"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", I will back you 100%. \n\nAre you free for a call around 7?\n\n## 2\n\n"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"I understand why it’s tempting to doubt large institutions—there are plenty of times throughout history when governments and official narratives haven"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"'t been honest. \n\nWhere the flat Earth idea falls apart for me, though, isn't about trusting"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" NASA or satellite imagery. It’s that you don't need space photos to observe curvature; humans figured this out thousands"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" of years ago with simple geometry. If the Earth were flat, lunar eclipses wouldn't consistently cast a round shadow"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", cargo ships wouldn't disappear bottom-first over the horizon, and you wouldn't see entirely different constellations as you travel"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" south of the equator. \n\nBeyond that, keeping something like this a secret would require literally millions of commercial pilots, navig"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ators, surveyors, and rival governments who hate each other to maintain the exact same lie for generations without a single leak. The simpler"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", physically consistent explanation is just that the world is a sphere.\n\n## 3\n\nThink of sunlight as looking white, but"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" actually containing every color of the rainbow mixed together. \n\nLight travels in waves, and different colors have different wave sizes"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":". Red light travels in long, lazy waves, while blue light travels in short, choppy, energetic waves.\n\nWhen"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" sunlight hits Earth, it has to pass through our atmosphere, which is packed full of tiny gas molecules—mostly nitrogen and oxygen. The"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" long, lazy red and yellow waves pass right through those molecules without bumping into them much. But the short, choppy blue waves are"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" almost the exact same size as the gas particles, so they run straight into them and bounce off in every possible direction. \n\nThis"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" bouncing is called *scattering*. When you look up during the day, you aren't seeing light beamed straight from the Sun"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"; you're seeing all that scattered blue light bouncing off the air above you and into your eyes. \n\n("}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"And here's a bonus: at sunset, the light has to travel through way more air to reach you, so all"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" the blue light scatters away before it gets to your eyes—leaving only the reds and oranges.)\n\n## 4\n\n雨"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"水敲击着窗玻璃，在昏黄的路灯光晕里织出一张细密而潮湿的"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"网。白日里喧闹的街巷此刻彻底沉寂下来，空旷的柏油路面倒映着斑驳的霓"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"虹，泛起清冷的光泽。晚风夹杂着泥土微凉的气息扑在脸上，偶尔有车辆碾过"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"积水，溅起短促的水声，旋即又归于平静。屋檐下水滴成线，滴滴答"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"答地丈量着夜的深度，将整座城市浸泡在一个宁静而清冽的梦境"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"里。\n\n## 5\n\nHi [Name],\n\nThanks so much for organizing this! Unfortunately, I won’t be able to make"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" it this Friday as I already have a prior commitment that evening. \n\nI hope you all have a great time unw"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"inding, and I'll catch you at the next one.\n\nBest,  \n[My Name]\n\n## 6"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nI aim for a clear, adaptable, and precise style that balances logical substance with a natural, conversational cadence."}}

